                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "1ecad371-3dba-43b2-b302-3f00b9cc96f4",
                        "entry_id": "f6d429f8-84da-3f72-a90c-49e777611863",
                        "tags": [],
                        "form": "Rai"
                    },
                    {
                        "form_id": "92628e5a-a5c8-4055-bae4-ac9bc16b9611",
                        "entry_id": "f6d429f8-84da-3f72-a90c-49e777611863",
                        "tags": [],
                        "form": "Raí"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "f19c9c64-6f5d-3925-a57c-5fd8c7e10d93",
                        "entry_id": "f6d429f8-84da-3f72-a90c-49e777611863",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Prénom masculin."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "166d2a56-557a-4e4f-8ea1-d43bafd5f077",
                                "sense_id": "f19c9c64-6f5d-3925-a57c-5fd8c7e10d93",
                                "text": "De quoi donner encore plus d’éclat à cette qualif en phase de poules, qui constitue « l’une des plus fortes émotions » de l’après-carrière pour Raï."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "6d3c4763-4020-4105-ba09-e04542079ead",
                                "sense_id": "f19c9c64-6f5d-3925-a57c-5fd8c7e10d93",
                                "text": "Grâce à ce soutien, Raï devint l’un des rares joueurs de football issu d’un club mineur à être appelé en Sélection Nationale Brésilienne."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "0901e0b9-e9d2-45ac-b62a-1b1e4f981433",
                                "sense_id": "f19c9c64-6f5d-3925-a57c-5fd8c7e10d93",
                                "text": "François Hollande a décoré jeudi, à Sao Paulo, l’ancien footballeur du Paris Saint-Germain, Raï Souza Vieira de Oliveira, de la Légion d’honneur."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [],
                "word_linkages": []
            },
            {
                "entry_id": "c6bea598-0672-3c3d-aab2-98f4bd11012b",
                "word": "raï",
                "pos": "noun",
                "lang_code": "fr",
                "forms": [],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "f1dd352e-a916-3467-9246-824920bc07b4",
                        "entry_id": "c6bea598-0672-3c3d-aab2-98f4bd11012b",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Genre musical algérien apparu au début du XXᵉ siècle dans la région de l’Oranie et popularisé en France depuis la fin des années 1980 par des immigrés algériens."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "86dfd6c4-254a-42ce-8929-1e1edff60966",
                                "sense_id": "f1dd352e-a916-3467-9246-824920bc07b4",
                                "text": "Qui a inventé le raï, le caftan, la fantasia ? Algérie et Maroc se livrent une inquiétante bataille culturelle. … Le raï, par exemple : honni en Algérie par les conservateurs, chassé, exilé en France, avec son lot de chanteurs tués et de répertoires « apurés » par l’islamisme, le voilà redevenu un porte-drapeau dans l’un et l’autre pays."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "5361982e-3eaa-4863-9e33-6205c79188a8",
                        "source_entry_id": "c6bea598-0672-3c3d-aab2-98f4bd11012b",
                        "source_sense_id": "f1dd352e-a916-3467-9246-824920bc07b4",
                        "target_lang_word": "Raï",
                        "target_lang_code": "de",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": []
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "4a1c4e40-7d66-48ee-86f6-740a5d2e77b3",
                        "source_entry_id": "c6bea598-0672-3c3d-aab2-98f4bd11012b",
                        "source_sense_id": "f1dd352e-a916-3467-9246-824920bc07b4",
                        "target_lang_word": "raï",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "raï",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "c888c2c1-0c81-357b-978b-146bd6727af4",
                                        "entry_id": "7155e90f-1054-3c30-bfce-e53696480f6f",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A form of music, originating in Oran, Algeria from Bedouin shepherds."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "44f854b0-f260-4214-b325-71a3b1be9779",
                                                "sense_id": "c888c2c1-0c81-357b-978b-146bd6727af4",
                                                "text": "Rai arrives in the US, in some ways, as the latest rage to hit the World Music record bins, the result of a new post-modern global marketing strategy."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e175f9be-9d42-49b9-9a77-0cbabe076979",
                                                "sense_id": "c888c2c1-0c81-357b-978b-146bd6727af4",
                                                "text": "1997: Karen Fog Olwig & Kirsten Hastrup, Siting Culture: The Shifting Anthropological Object — chapter 3: “Which world? On the diffusion of Algerian raï to the West” (by Marc Schade-Poulsen), p59: INTRODUCTION →ISBN (10); →ISBN (13))^†\nThis chapter deals with raï music from Algeria. Since its emergence in the late 1970s, raï has spread throughout the world and stands today as an exponent of “World Music”. The chapter traces a transnational process that has taken place in the 1980s: the diffusion of raï from the cabarets of Oran (the second largest city of Algeria) to the stereo racks in the West. It evokes the existence of different places and spaces for the consumption of raï."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "d7f9f96d-822c-473c-bdae-0ff952c8ee55",
                                                "sense_id": "c888c2c1-0c81-357b-978b-146bd6727af4",
                                                "text": "In France, raï’s lack of commercial success was thought to have been caused by hidden French racism and the subsequent de facto absence of raï on commercial radio and prime-time television. All in all, it did seem difficult to “sell an Arab” to a Western audience, as was the case, for example, with Cheb Mami’s U.S.-recorded album “Let me raï”, released during the Gulf War."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "f746d3cc-5c2c-43ee-aed2-34dbd961b54d",
                                                "sense_id": "c888c2c1-0c81-357b-978b-146bd6727af4",
                                                "text": "The rise of raï has paralleled the rise of Islamism in Algerian society, despite its mixing the male and female roles of musical production and consumption. Indeed, the paradox is at first glance perplexing because one might expect the critical message of raï to be anti-Islamist. The rhetoric of raï, however, does not contradict the rise of Islamism in Algeria, and therefore it acquires the potential to complement religious fundamentalism. Raï and Islam do not so much occupy the same space as draw a cluster of public discussions and debates about gender into the same discourse (Schade-Poulsen 1996, 148–53; compare Bohlman 2000, 293–96)."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "6ff6165f-e270-490d-abbc-d4555e7f9e18",
                                                "sense_id": "c888c2c1-0c81-357b-978b-146bd6727af4",
                                                "text": "At least three conflicting varieties of Raï drifted in through the open doorway of the bus, blasting from cafés in the square."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
